Charts may be drawn in a window using one of two methods.  These are:

1) Display Charts Using Draw Mode
   ==============================

This is a direct draw method which displays the chart as it is being built.
Anytime the chart needs to be updated or refreshed, it is redrawn.  For 
example, this method would show the slices of a pie or bars in a bar chart 
being generated to the window.

2) Display Charts Using Bitmap Mode
   ================================

This is a bitmap draw method which displays the chart as a bitmap.  This
means the chart is generated to an off screen bitmap and saved.  Upon 
completion, the chart is displayed to the window in a bitblt.  

Anytime the chart needs to be updated or refreshed, the bitmap is
updated.  This means the chart is never redrawn and the result is a faster 
redraw or refresh time.


